AB  - Providing life on Earth with air is one of the most fundamental requirements. Thus, the quality of air affects life on Earth to a large extent. Air quality in the concerned city of Amravati is degrading, presenting a significant hazard to the residents. Three monitoring stations in Amravati city, including the residential area, the industrial area, and the commercial area, were used in this study to analyze the average daily concentrations of Respirable Suspended Particulate Matter (RSPM-PM10), nitrogen oxides (NOx), sulfur dioxide (SO2). In recent years, resource utilization needs have increased dramatically, resulting in a change in the chemical composition of the air in the atmosphere. These pollution parameters and meteorological parameters are collected for Amravati City from 2008 to 2018. To analyze the ambient air quality present at three stations in the study area by assessing the following: Annual Variations of pollutants; Seasonal Variations of pollutants; Exceedance factor; Meteorological Parameters Correlation Analysis and Wind rose Diagram. This study uses an Artificial Neural Network (ANN) model called LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) to predict pollution parameters. Based on past data of 10 years, i.e., 2008-2018, the pollution parameters for 2019 are calculated using MATLAB software. Compared with the actual monitoring of the data, this model gives very desirable results.
